---
const stats = [
  { value: "1900s", label: "Roadhouse roots" },
  { value: "1940s", label: "At our current home" },
  { value: "2015", label: "Renovated & reborn" },
  { value: "25", label: "Wing sauces & flavors" },
];
---

<section id="about" class="py-20 md:py-32 bg-[#2A1C0E]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Section Header -->
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <span class="text-[#D4622A] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sm">Our Story</span>
      <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl text-gold-gradient mt-2 mb-4">
        ABOUT THE VAN REED INN
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center mb-16">
      <!-- Copy -->
      <div class="space-y-5 text-[#F5F0E8]/80 leading-relaxed text-lg">
        <p>
          The Van Reed Inn is a true Berks County original. This old roadhouse traces its
          roots to the early 1900s and has stood at its current home on Bernville Road
          since the 1940s, serving generations of Reading and Leesport locals. In 2015 it
          was completely renovated and reopened, and today the Van Reed is what every
          neighborhood bar should be — friendly faces, cold beer, and food that's far
          better than it has any right to be.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything here is made fresh, in-house. The smoker is the heart of the kitchen:
          pork, brisket, and our famous jumbo wings all get their time in the smoke before
          they hit your plate. The wings — smoked low and slow, then deep fried crispy and
          tossed in your pick of 19 house sauces or 6 premium flavors — are why folks
          around here call them the best wings in Berks County. The award-winning smoked
          chili, loaded with five savory meats, has its own loyal following.
        </p>
        <p>
          Just up the road from Reading Regional Airport on Route 183, we're an easy stop
          whether you're grabbing lunch, catching the game, shooting a round of pool, or
          picking up wings and a 6-pack to go. Dine in, take out, or pull up a stool and
          stay awhile — at the Van Reed, you're a regular by your second visit.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Image -->
      <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-[#D4A574]/20">
        <img
          src="/images/bar-interior.jpg"
          alt="Our bar with the full tap lineup and game on the TVs"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover img-zoom"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Stats -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
      {stats.map(stat => (
        <div class="text-center p-6 bg-[#3D2914] rounded-xl border border-[#D4A574]/20">
          <div class="font-display text-4xl text-gold-gradient mb-1">{stat.value}</div>
          <div class="text-[#F5F0E8]/60 text-sm">{stat.label}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
